  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason includes outcome-reference differences and their probability-weighted mean. However, the individual only refers to computing and comparing expected values, which, while mathematically equivalent to the mean difference in this case (since the reference is zero), is conceptually distinct. The reason emphasizes a reference-dependent evaluation of gains, whereas the individual’s report reflects a standard expected value calculation without any indication of reference dependence or psychological framing of outcomes as differences. The justification is based on a normative economic rule (expected value maximization), not on the specific cognitive mechanism implied by the decision reason (reference-dependent differences). Therefore, although the numerical computation overlaps, there is no evidence that the individual used the conceptual framework of the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 30
